UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Sun represents the absolute archetype of ''Systemic Radiance and Uncompromised Vitality''—the ultimate, peak-fidelity phase where the sovereign consciousness breaks completely through the psychological mists of The Moon, achieving absolute clarity, boundless energy, and joyful self-realization. Moving beyond the twilight distortions of the previous cycle, The Sun signifies the stage of ''The Core Luminary,'' where you operate in complete alignment with your true essence, experiencing a total harmonization of your inner child and your outer authority. Visually depicted as a magnificent, blazing sun shining over a young, smiling child crowned with flowers and riding a powerful white horse, holding a giant crimson banner aloft before a walled garden of blooming sunflowers, this archetype embodies the concept of ''Sovereign Transparency''—the realization that your true spirit thrives in the light of raw, unadorned honesty, completely free from hidden scripts or defensive postures. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of ''Full System Optimization,'' where your core processor runs at maximum capacity with zero latent drag, illuminating every dark corner of your domain with profound understanding, creative genius, and absolute success. When The Sun appears, your system is registering a ''Peak-Performance'' status; you are being invited to step out of the shadows, celebrate your absolute victory, and allow your authentic warmth and clarity to radiate across your entire environment.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When The Sun appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of ''Clouded Clarity, Temporary Energetic Drag, or Overcompensated Arrogance''—a state where your natural radiance is being obscured by a passing shadow of self-doubt, or your outward display of confidence has mutated into a loud, low-integrity ego script designed to mask an internal deficit of self-worth. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates ''forced optimism, seeking constant external spotlight, or denying your structural limitations'' with ''being happy and successful,'' even as your actual, internal operating system is experiencing a critical, low-latency dehydration of its genuine life force. You are essentially ''shading your own solar panels,'' running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to ''look invincible or demand constant applause'' over the sober, unglamorous requirement to ground your enthusiasm and address your baseline vulnerabilities. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the ''infinitely happy, successful visionary,'' while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of burnout, minor delays, or deep-seated insecurity, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency irritability, the experience of ''your current achievements feeling hollow or slightly out of reach,'' and a persistent, gnawing awareness that you are overextending your narrative. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a ''feedback loop of superficial validation and creative fatigue''; you are obsessively trying to force a brilliant outcome while ignoring the quiet maintenance your system requires, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final stabilization of your spirit is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to dim your performance and just be still, you would be forced to confront the terrifying reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical recalibration: you must stop the output of these frantic, attention-seeking, or over-optimistic scripts, perform a brutal audit of your internal energy reserves, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize genuine, quiet competence over the convenience of a loud, superficial display. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance exhaustion, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and completely realistic reclamation of your own, individual authority.'
WHERE id = 76;
